    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d149">

                <pb facs="0158" n="146" sameAs="frus:frus1946v08/pg146"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Japan)/2–2546</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the State–War–Navy Coordinating
                        Committee to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">SWN–3920</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-02-25">25 February 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">Subject: Basic Directive for Post-Surrender Military
                    Government in Japan Proper.</p>
                <table>
                    <row role="label">
                        <cell>References:</cell>
                        <cell><hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>. SWNCC 52/8/D</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell/>
                        <cell><hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>. SWNCC 52/9</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell/>
                        <cell><hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>. SWNCC 52/10</cell>
                    </row>
                </table>
                <p>By informal action on 25 February 1946 the State–War–Navy Coordinating Committee
                    approved SWNCC 52/9, a copy of which is enclosed.<anchor n="94" xml:id="d149-f1"
                    /></p>
                <p>In approving this paper the Committee agreed that the original and revised
                    instructions of the Joint Chiefs of Staff to General MacArthur recommended by
                    the State–War–Navy Coordinating Committee be made available to the Far Eastern
                    Commission.</p>
                <p>It is requested that these instructions, contained in Appendices “A” and “B” of
                    the approved paper, be transmitted to the Far Eastern Commission by the State
                        Department.<anchor n="95" xml:id="d149-f2"/></p>
                <p>The Joint Chiefs of Staff on 14 February 1946 advised General MacArthur that the
                    messages contained in Appendices “A” and “B” were being made available to the
                    Far Eastern Commission.</p>
                <closer>For the State–War–Navy Coordinating Committee:<lb/><signed><hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">H. Freeman Matthews</hi></signed><lb/><hi
                        rendition="#italic">Acting Chairman</hi></closer>




                <xi:include href="d149-a1.xml" xpointer="d149-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d149-a2.xml" xpointer="d149-a2"/>
            </div>
